---
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro'
import { CONTACT, NAME } from '../constants'
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'

/*
 * Written from what the app actually does (checked in its code on 19 November 2026).
 * When the app starts talking to anyone new, this page changes in the same commit.
 */
const services = [
  {
    name: 'radio-browser.info',
    href: 'https://www.radio-browser.info/',
    what: 'The lists of stations for a genre or a country, and your searches.',
  },
  {
    name: 'The radio stations themselves',
    href: '',
    what: 'The music and the song title, straight from the station you picked. Each station runs its own server, with its own rules.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Apple’s iTunes Search',
    href: 'https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/',
    what: 'When a song is playing, its artist and title are looked up here to find the album and its cover.',
  },
  {
    name: 'This site, minkefm.fifthguild.com',
    href: '/',
    what: 'Once a week, a fresh list of stations to fall back on when the station directory is down. The app only downloads it.',
  },
  {
    name: 'LRCLIB',
    href: 'https://lrclib.net/',
    what: 'The same artist and title, to find the lyrics.',
  },
]
---

<Layout title={`Privacy · ${NAME}`} description={`What ${NAME} keeps about you (nothing), what stays on your phone, and who the app talks to.`}>
  <Nav />
  <main class="wrap privacy">
    <article class="privacy__sheet panel">
      <p class="eyebrow">Last changed 19 November 2026</p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="privacy__lead">
        {NAME} has no account, no analytics and no ads. Nothing you do in the app is sent to us, so we have nothing about you to keep, sell or lose.
      </p>

      <h2>What stays on your phone</h2>
      <p>So it can pick up where you left off, the app keeps these on your phone, and only there:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your favourite stations</li>
        <li>the last station you played and its volume</li>
        <li>the songs you have heard, with the time</li>
        <li>station lists it has already downloaded, so they open quickly</li>
        <li>the skin you picked, and the sleep timer while it runs</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Deleting the app deletes all of it.</p>

      <h2>Who the app talks to</h2>
      <p>
        To play radio, the app connects to these services directly from your phone. We are not in between. Like any server, each one sees your phone’s IP address
        and what the app asked for.
      </p>
      <dl class="privacy__services">
        {
          services.map(s => (
            <div>
              <dt>{s.href ? <a href={s.href}>{s.name}</a> : s.name}</dt>
              <dd>{s.what}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
      <p>They get nothing else: no name, no account, no ID for your phone. The app’s fonts are built in, so no font service is involved.</p>

      <h2>Permissions</h2>
      <p>
        On Android, the app asks to show a notification. That notification is the player, with the station and buttons to pause or skip, and it lets the radio
        keep playing with the screen off. On iPhone and Android the app plays audio in the background for the same reason. It asks for nothing else: no location,
        contacts or microphone.
      </p>

      <h2>This site</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets no cookies. The skin you pick here is saved in your browser and goes nowhere else. Cloudflare hosts the site and keeps short request logs to
        run and protect it. Visits are counted with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which uses no cookies and doesn’t track you across sites.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>The app collects nothing from anyone, including children.</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {NAME} is made by Fifth Guild, in Serbia. Questions about this page go to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>, and we reply within a few days. You can also
        complain to the data protection authority where you live.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If the app ever starts keeping or sending anything new, this page will say so first, with a new date at the top.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy {
    padding-block: clamp(16px, 4vw, 40px) clamp(56px, 8vw, 96px);
  }
  .privacy__sheet {
    max-width: 780px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: clamp(28px, 6vw, 64px);
  }
  .privacy__sheet h1 {
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    color: var(--card-ink);
  }
  .privacy__sheet h2 {
    margin: 44px 0 14px;
    color: var(--card-ink);
    font-size: clamp(25px, 3vw, 32px);
  }
  html[data-skin='lcd'] .privacy__sheet h2 {
    font-size: clamp(18px, 2.2vw, 22px);
  }
  .privacy__sheet p + p,
  .privacy__sheet ul + p,
  .privacy__sheet dl + p {
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  .privacy__sheet .eyebrow {
    color: var(--card-dim);
  }
  .privacy__lead {
    font-size: clamp(19px, 2vw, 22px);
  }
  .privacy__sheet ul {
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
  }
  .privacy__services {
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
    margin: 18px 0 0;
  }
  .privacy__services div {
    padding-left: 16px;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--card-link);
  }
  .privacy__services dt {
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .privacy__services dd {
    margin: 2px 0 0;
    color: var(--card-dim);
  }
</style>
